Package: zulm
Title: Tensor Graphs, Training and Inference on 'ggml'
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Pedro", "Baltazar", , "pedrobtz@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Builds computation graphs of tensors in R, runs them on the
    CPU, differentiates them and trains their parameters, through the
    'ggml' tensor library (<https://github.com/ggml-org/ggml>) bundled in
    its CPU subset. Graphs are built once per input shape and run many
    times; the same operations train small and medium neural networks
    with the AdamW and SGD optimisers and run pretrained transformer
    checkpoints read from 'GGUF' or 'safetensors' files. Results
    reproduce bit for bit at a fixed seed whatever the thread count.
    A versioned C interface lets other packages build models on top.
